@issuer = http://localhost:8080
@scimToken = corridor-scim-token

### Liveness
GET {{issuer}}/healthz

### Admin console
GET {{issuer}}/

### OIDC discovery
GET {{issuer}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### JWKS (two kids: current + retired)
GET {{issuer}}/jwks

### Authorize, portal confidential client (renders login form without login_hint)
# GET {{issuer}}/authorize?client_id=portal&redirect_uri=http://localhost:5200/signin-oidc&response_type=code&scope=openid%20profile&state=demo-state

### Authorize, spa public client with PKCE S256 (challenge = base64url(sha256(verifier)))
# GET {{issuer}}/authorize?client_id=spa&redirect_uri=http://localhost:5173/callback&response_type=code&scope=openid%20profile&code_challenge=CHALLENGE&code_challenge_method=S256&login_hint=inspector@corridor.example&state=demo-state&nonce=demo-nonce

### Token exchange, confidential client via Basic auth
# POST {{issuer}}/token
# Authorization: Basic cG9ydGFsOmNvcnJpZG9yLXBvcnRhbC1zZWNyZXQ=
# Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
#
# grant_type=authorization_code&code=THE_CODE&redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5000%2Fsignin-oidc

### Token exchange, spa public client with PKCE verifier
# POST {{issuer}}/token
# Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
#
# grant_type=authorization_code&code=THE_CODE&client_id=spa&redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5173%2Fcallback&code_verifier=THE_VERIFIER

### Legacy service token (client credentials)
POST {{issuer}}/token
Authorization: Basic bGVnYWN5OmNvcnJpZG9yLWxlZ2FjeS1zZWNyZXQ=
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

### Userinfo (paste a bearer token)
# GET {{issuer}}/userinfo
# Authorization: Bearer THE_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Logout with registered post-logout redirect
# GET {{issuer}}/logout?client_id=portal&post_logout_redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5000%2F&state=demo-state

### SAML IdP metadata
GET {{issuer}}/saml/metadata

### SCIM: list users
GET {{issuer}}/scim/v2/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{scimToken}}

### SCIM: filtered list
GET {{issuer}}/scim/v2/Users?filter=userName%20eq%20%22officer%40corridor.example%22
Authorization: Bearer {{scimToken}}

### SCIM: create a user
POST {{issuer}}/scim/v2/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{scimToken}}
Content-Type: application/scim+json

{
  "schemas": ["urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:User", "urn:corridor:scim:1.0:User"],
  "userName": "analyst@corridor.example",
  "displayName": "Rosa Kellerman",
  "active": true,
  "groups": [{ "display": "trace-reviewers" }],
  "urn:corridor:scim:1.0:User": { "role": "Clerk" }
}

### SCIM: patch (replace active)
# PATCH {{issuer}}/scim/v2/Users/THE_ID
# Authorization: Bearer {{scimToken}}
# Content-Type: application/scim+json
#
# { "schemas": ["urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:PatchOp"], "Operations": [{ "op": "replace", "path": "active", "value": false }] }

### XACML PDP: Officer reads trace cases -> Permit
POST {{issuer}}/pdp/decide
Content-Type: application/xacml+xml

<Request xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:2.0:context:schema:os">
  <Subject>
    <Attribute AttributeId="urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:2.0:subject:role">
      <AttributeValue>Officer</AttributeValue>
    </Attribute>
  </Subject>
  <Resource>
    <Attribute AttributeId="urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:1.0:resource:resource-id">
      <AttributeValue>trace-cases</AttributeValue>
    </Attribute>
  </Resource>
  <Action>
    <Attribute AttributeId="urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:1.0:action:action-id">
      <AttributeValue>read</AttributeValue>
    </Attribute>
  </Action>
</Request>
